# Spec development

Task status lives in #54 (application), #82 (risk API), and #32 (HMI).
Dotdog workflow improvements are tracked in #86.

1. Query the observed map and read the affected spec, [ADR](../../docs/adrs/README.md), and owning ticket.
2. Specify acceptance and shared-boundary changes before implementing.
3. Implement and run the relevant domain tests; add source scopes for new areas.
4. Stage new files, run `bun run dog:map`, then `bun run dog:check`.
5. For each reported spec area, review the source diff and update the spec and ADR if needed.
   A behavior-preserving edit can keep the prose; explain that in the PR.
6. Acknowledge only reviewed areas with `bun run dog:review Contracts Shared`
   (substitute the actual names), then remap and check again.
7. Include spec, code, and review-hash changes in the same PR. CI must pass;
   a passing hash check is not evidence that domain tests or live checks passed.
